Subject: [PATCH] arc: use full-width moves for syscall argument registers

The ARC700 MOV_S encoding cannot move between r4/r5 or r5/r6.
Use the full-width instruction, which supports these registers on
both ARC700 and ARCv2.

Signed-off-by: lean <chenlin@fnnas.com>

--- a/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/arc/syscall.S
+++ b/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/arc/syscall.S
@@ -24,8 +24,8 @@
 	mov_s	r1, r2
 	mov_s	r2, r3
 	mov_s	r3, r4
-	mov_s	r4, r5
-	mov_s	r5, r6
+	mov	r4, r5
+	mov	r5, r6
 
 	ARC_TRAP_INSN
 	brhi	r0, -4096, L (call_syscall_err)
